; Ellerman, "On Double-Entry Bookkeeping: The Mathematical Treatment",
; Accounting Education 23:5 (2014), pp. 496-498: the vector journal over
; three property types, with transaction 2b routed through Equity "for
; simplicity, directly with equity rather than using income statement or
; property-flow accounts" (p. 497).  The balances are p. 498's ending row,
; (10200, 35, 20) (-9200, 0, 0) (-1000, -35, -20), which sums to zero in
; each property type.  The same journal is a kernel-checked golden in the
; ledger-semantics oracle (namespace Ledger.Ellerman).

2014/01/01 Beginning vector balance sheet
    Assets          $9000
    Assets          40 WIDGET
    Assets          50 HALF
    Liabilities     $-10000
    Equity          $1000
    Equity          -40 WIDGET
    Equity          -50 HALF

2014/01/02 1. inputs used
    Assets          -30 HALF
    Equity          30 HALF

2014/01/03 2a. widgets produced
    Assets          15 WIDGET
    Equity          -15 WIDGET

2014/01/04 2b. widgets sold, Ellerman's encoding
    Assets          $2000
    Assets          -20 WIDGET
    Equity          20 WIDGET
    Equity          $-2000

2014/01/05 3. loan principal
    Assets          $-800
    Liabilities     $800

test bal --flat
              $10200
             20 HALF
           35 WIDGET  Assets
              $-1000
            -20 HALF
          -35 WIDGET  Equity
              $-9200  Liabilities
